Ivabradine tablets are a medicament in measured doses for retail sale, so they fall in heading 3004. Ivabradine is a benzazepine derivative, with a 3-benzazepin-2-one structure. That puts it in subheading 3004.90 (other), not in the antibiotic, hormone, or alkaloid subheadings. I recall CBP rulings on ivabradine (Corlanor) classifying it under 3004.90.9290, but I have not verified this.

The 3004.90 statistical suffixes include 3004.90.92 ("Other: Other") with 90 for other. I'm not certain whether 3004.90.9290 or 3004.90.9250 is correct. I'm going with 3004.90.9290.

{"hts_code": "3004.90.9290", "reason": "Ivabradine tablets are a packaged medicament of mixed or unmixed products in measured doses for retail sale for treating heart failure, falling in HTSUS 3004.90 as an 'other' medicament."}
